            <ArticleTitle>Septic arthritis of the temporomandibular joint in a 6-year-old child.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>242-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Septic arthritis of the temporomandibular joint (TMJ) is rare, and is almost exclusively confined to adults; we know of only four cases previously described in children. We present a 6-year-old girl who had septic arthritis of the temporomandibular joint with no obvious cause. We stress the need for prompt diagnosis and intervention to prevent serious consequences.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
